======================== what that adds up to ========================

Twenty-eight added lines in total, no removed line and no changed line. Two
per Model object, in both files, and nothing outside a Properties70 block.
Every existing property, object number, name, transform, geometry array,
material colour and connection is at the same place with the same value.

fcad-legacy.fbx, fcad-identity-escaping.fbx and fcad-renamed.fbx are new
artefacts and have no baseline to differ from: the first is the pair the legacy
policy is measured with, the second carries the definition keys chosen to break
the identity grammar, and the third is the neutral test variant the Unity
measurement uses — the same identities under different designations, built by
naming different strings and not by any reimport, which this build does not
have. None of them replaces a committed file.

======================= the measurement inputs did not move ====================

The §22B-1e2a and §22B-1e2b documents are written by the same production writer
through `fbx_channel_documents` and `fbx_identity_variants`, and those two
examples hand their synthetic documents `ExportDefinitionIdentity::Unrecorded`
and `ExportOccurrence::Unrecorded`, so they carry no identity property at all.
Both examples were run from this branch and from a clean worktree of
origin/main and compared file for file:

  diff -rq  fbx_channel_documents   before/after   ->  no differences (13 files)
  diff -rq  fbx_identity_variants   before/after   ->  no differences (10 files)

The recorded editor runs of those two measurements are therefore still runs of
the bytes they were taken from, and no historical conclusion has been rewritten
under this slice's code.
